---
description: Provide accessible contextual help from the upper-left of every application area
alwaysApply: true
---

# Contextual Page Help

- Every page and functional section must expose a visible question-mark help button at its upper-left edge in the RTL layout.
- The help control must not disturb the true center alignment of the header title.
- Opening help must show guidance specific to the current page or section, not generic placeholder text.
- Explain the area's purpose, fields, actions, normal workflow, required permissions, important accounting or inventory effects, validation errors, and irreversible operations.
- Help content must stay synchronized whenever the related feature or business rule changes.
- The button and help surface must be keyboard accessible, mobile friendly, and have a clear Persian accessible label.
- Use an adequate touch target and prevent overlap with headers, navigation, modals, and mobile controls.
- Do not add inactive help buttons, unfinished text, or fabricated instructions.
